{"kind":"stack","id":"soils-rocks-organic","title":"Soils: rocks and organic matter","theme":{"background":"#f4efe6","foreground":"#2b2118","font":"Georgia, serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-t","content":"Weathering"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-e","content":"The slow breaking down of rocks into smaller pieces by wind, rain, ice and plant roots."},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-t","content":"Organic matter"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-e","content":"Material that was once part of a living thing, such as dead leaves, roots and animal waste."},{"type":"button","id":"c2-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"Which of these is the main source of the rock particles in soil?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"Rocks broken into small pieces","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"Clouds","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"Sea water","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"What is the name for the part of soil made from dead plants and animals?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"Organic matter","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"Bedrock","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-c","label":"Magma","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-d","label":"Gravel","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-t","content":"You are digging in a garden and find dark, crumbly soil. Do you test it for rock pieces first, or look for worms and dead leaves?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a","label":"Test for rock pieces","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"Look for worms and leaves","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"You sieve the soil and find tiny grains of sand and stone. Those came from rocks breaking down over many years."},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"You find worms and rotting leaves. These are organic matter, which helps the soil hold water and feed plants."},{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-q","content":"Which pair describes what good garden soil is made from?"},{"type":"button","id":"c8-a","label":"Rock particles and organic matter","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"Water and air only","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-c","label":"Metal and glass","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"Which of these is an example of organic matter?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a","label":"A fallen oak leaf","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"A piece of granite","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-c","label":"A grain of sand","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-d","label":"A drop of rain","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"What do rock particles give soil?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"Its texture and minerals","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"Its colour of leaves","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"Its flowers","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-q","content":"Which is bigger in most soils, rock particles or organic matter?"},{"type":"button","id":"c11-a","label":"Rock particles","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c12"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c11-b","label":"Organic matter","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c12"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c12","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c12-h","content":"Well done: you know what soil is made from."},{"type":"text","id":"c12-m","content":"Soil is a mix of broken rock and organic matter. Keep looking closely at the ground around you."}],"actions":[]}}
